sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant C as Customer
    participant G as API Gateway
    participant T as Transfer Service
    participant D as Ledger Database
    C->>G: POST /transfers + auth + Idempotency-Key
    G->>G: Validate token/session, quotas
    G->>T: Authenticated principal and request
    T->>T: Check source ownership, recipient, amount, limits, step-up
    T->>D: BEGIN; acquire appropriate locks / serialize balance
    T->>D: Check unique idempotency key and request fingerprint
    alt Key already committed with same request
        D-->>T: Existing transfer result
        T-->>G: Original outcome (no new ledger write)
    else Key reused with different request
        D-->>T: Fingerprint mismatch
        T-->>G: Conflict (no ledger write)
    else New authorized transfer
        T->>D: Check available funds and enforce limits
        T->>D: Post balanced debit and credit + durable key/result
        T->>D: INSERT audit outbox event in same DB transaction
        T->>D: COMMIT
        D-->>T: Transfer committed
        T-->>G: Transaction ID + status
    end
    G-->>C: Response over TLS
    Note over D: A worker later delivers committed outbox events to append-only audit storage
